                                    <h2><span class="shaft"><img id="1041-0" src="//cdn.recordinghacks.com/images/icons/patterns/icon_8.png" width=27 height=27 alt="Bidirectional" title="Bidirectional" ><img id="1041-1" src="//cdn.recordinghacks.com/images/icons/patterns/icon_sg.png" width=27 height=27 alt="Shotgun" title="Shotgun" ><img id="1041-2" src="//cdn.recordinghacks.com/images/icons/patterns/icon_xy.png" width=27 height=27 alt="X/Y Stereo" title="X/Y Stereo" ><img id="1041-3" src="//cdn.recordinghacks.com/images/icons/patterns/icon_ms.png" width=27 height=27 alt="Mid-Side Stereo" title="Mid-Side Stereo" ></span>Audio-Technica BP4029</h2>
                    
                    <h2 class="sub">                    Multi-Pattern Condenser Microphone</h2>
                    <p>The BP4029 is a revised version of Audio-Technica&#8217;s AT835ST. Both are ~9-inch stereo shotgun microphones with a pair of electret condenser elements.</p><p>Like its predecessor, the BP4029 has two capsules &#8212; one line-gradient and one bidirectional. The output from these two is available independently via the XLR5M connector, to be matrixed externally into mid-side stereo. </p><p>The mic also has an onboard matrix that can produce two varieties of L/R stereo, &#8220;narrow&#8221; and &#8220;wide.&#8221; These three stereo modes are selected via a switch on the microphone.</p><p>A second switch enables a high-pass filter (-12dB/octave @ 80Hz).</p><p>The mic is RoHS compliant &#8212; free of hazardous substances.</p><p>It ships with a 2&#39; breakout cable (XLR5F to 2xXLR3M), a stand clamp (p/n AT8405a), a foam windscreen (p/n AT8134), a thread adapter for 3/8&#39;&#39;-16 mic stands, and a carrying case (p/n SG2).<p>Permalink: <a href="//recordinghacks.com/microphones/Audio-Technica/BP4029">Audio-Technica BP4029</a></p>
